  Placement: 1
  CardStory: "How they writhe within me. Ever squirming, twisting around my spine,
    miniscule hooks and burrs sharing my nerves and stem with divinity itself. And
    though my body is diminished, the blessing doesn\u2019t render it less. \r\n\r\nI
    am heightened by their consumption, and in sharing what I am with the Holy Father
    I lose myself and become more in the heartbeat. But I don\u2019t have a pulse
    anymore. The bindings wrap around my viscera, constraining my heart, my guts.
    Not mine, because I will be no more.\r\n\r\nThe body dissolves, every fiber and
    scrap of tissue and sinew and through weaving and twinning and screaming in exquisite
    pain. No truer worship than to become the vessel for His will. I can feel myself
    **unravel.** "
